   "text": "Thanks, Ben. You're verified.\n\nI checked order 9501 from Pho Real, and you were charged only once. The order total is $33.67, and the payment record shows:\n\n- **Authorization hold, $33.67 (placed 6:02 PM):** This is a temporary hold the bank places when an order is made. It was released when the order was charged, and its status is \"voided.\"\n- **Settled charge, $33.67 (6:47 PM):** This is the actual charge.\n\nThe hold is probably the second $33.67 you're seeing in your bank app. It's not a second charge, and it should drop off your statement within 1 to 3 business days. Because you were only charged once, there's no refund to issue.\n\nIf you still see two settled charges after a few business days, or you see a charge for an order you didn't place, let me know and I can look into it further. Is there anything else I can help with?"
